          "kind": "figure",
          "src": "content/media/architecture.svg",
          "alt": "SafeProof architecture. The accused identifier is blinded into a tag, from which the reporter derives a nullifier. Evidence is committed with a salt and stays on the device. The report proof is posted to the ledger's nullifier set and commitment log. A threshold proof over k distinct nullifiers reveals only the count to an intermediary, who can send a consent-based invitation."
